Better make .container padding left/right 0 and rely on .hero padding. Or set .container { padding:0; } and let inner sections manage. Simpler: set .container { padding:0 var(--space-4); box-sizing:border-box; } Already there.

But overflow still 410 vs 390 > 20px. Might be due to button min-height causing width? Buttons are inline-block with min-height but width auto content; plus gap var(--space-4) (16px) between two buttons. So total width of button plus gap maybe exceed container width? The text length "Book a consultation" (20 chars) may cause button width wide. On mobile, maybe should stack vertically. Could add media query to make hero button container flex-direction column on small screens (already added .hero > div flex-direction column in CSS earlier). But the selector .hero > div may not match because the flex container is not a direct child? In Home, we have <section className="hero"><h1>...</h1><p>...</p><div style={...}>buttons</div></section>. The div is inside .hero; .hero > div matches that. However CSS added earlier had .hero > div { flex-direction: column; } within media query max-width:420px but we only added at bottom after ensuring overflow but didn't include flex-direction column property? At earlier edit we added .hero > div { flex-direction: column; } inside media query? We have:

@media (max-width: 420px) {
  .hero > div {
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .hero > div > a,
  .hero > div > button {
    width: 100%;
    text-align: center;
  }
}

But after we changed button back to Link, the selector .hero > div > button no longer applies; we need .hero > div > a to set width, which we have. The container still flex-direction column, should stack and width 100% (with padding). The link's width 100% plus container padding may still overflow? 100% width plus padding inside container leads to overflow. But width:100% on a block-level element with box-sizing: content-box also adds padding? No we set width:100% on a (inline-block?) Not sure.

Simplify: In CSS for small screens, set .hero > div > a { display:block; width:auto; max-width:100%; } maybe not important.

But test also expects "Explore services" to be a link with href "/services". So we changed back to Link.

Now fix container overflow: set .container { box-sizing:border-box; padding:0 var(--space-4); max-width:100%; }

