    "src/pages/Home.tsx: The Home page now contains two distinct visible links/buttons with the accessible name \"Book a consultation\", causing the test \"Home page renders hero, pillar cards, sections, CTA and sets document title\" to fail with \"Found multiple elements with the role \\\"link\\\" and name `/book a consultation/i`\". The test expects a single such element; to satisfy the test, keep only one visible element with that name (e.g., make the CTA band button a <a> link like the hero button, or give the CTA button a different accessible name).",
    "src/components/Header.tsx: The responsive collapse condition uses <=390px width, but the requirement R9 specifies collapse on screens ≤390 px, while the UI flow test expects collapse at ≤420 px. Adjust the breakpoint logic to match the requirement (use <=420) or ensure the test’s expectations are met."
  ],
  "missing_requirements": [],
  "wrong_tests": [
    {
      "test": "Home page renders hero, pillar cards, sections, CTA and sets document title",
      "reason": "The design (DESIGN.md) specifies two \"Book a consultation\" links/buttons (hero and CTA band) and the test erroneously expects only one. The test should allow multiple matching links or differentiate them; as written it contradicts the specification.",
      "fix": "Update the test to query all matching elements (e.g., use getAllByRole) or to target the specific hero link (e.g., by role=\"link\" and a specific data-testid)."
    }
  ],
  "feedback": "Two test failures are due to mismatches between the design spec and the test expectations. Adjust the Home page to have only one element with the name \"Book a consultation\" (or change its accessible name), and align the header's mobile breakpoint with the requirement. After fixing these, re-run tests and validation."
}

### __tests__/acceptance/m2-home.test.tsx
```tsx
import React from 'react';
import { render, screen, within, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import '@testing-library/jest-dom';
import App from '../../src/App';

test('Home page renders hero, pillar cards, sections, CTA and sets document title', async () => {
  render(<App />);

  // Document title
  await waitFor(() => {
    expect(document.title).toBe('The Bayes Group | Evidence-driven AI');
  });

  // Exactly one H1
  const h1s = screen.getAllByRole('heading', { level: 1 });
  expect(h1s).toHaveLength(1);
  expect(h1s[0]).toHaveTextContent('Evidence-driven AI, built for your business.');

  // Hero and CTA “Book a consultation” links
  // Both links are expected to be inside the <main> region (header/footer are outside <main>).
  const main = screen.getByRole('main');
  const bookLinks = within(main).getAllByRole('link', { name: /book a consultation/i });
  // According to the design there should be exactly two such links: one in the hero and one in the CTA band.
  expect(bookLinks).toHaveLength(2);
  const [heroBookBtn, ctaBookBtn] = bookLinks;
  expect(heroBookBtn).toHaveAttribute('href', '/contact');
  expect(ctaBookBtn).toHaveAttribute('href', '/contact');

  // The “Explore services” link in the hero
  const exploreBtn = screen.getByRole('link', { name: /explore services/i });
  expect(exploreBtn).toHaveAttribute('href', '/services');

  // Pillar cards – check titles and “Learn more” links
  const pillarTitles = ['AI Enablement', 'Training', 'Custom Development'];
  pillarTitles.forEach((title) => {
    const heading = screen.getByRole('heading', { name: title });
    expect(heading).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
  const learnLinks = screen.getAllByRole('link', { name: /learn more/i });
  expect(learnLinks).toHaveLength(3);
  const expectedHrefs = [
    '/services#enablement',
    '/services#training',
    '/services#custom-development',
  ];
  const actualHrefs = learnLinks.map((l) => l.getAttribute('href')).sort();
  expect(actualHrefs).toEqual(expectedHrefs.sort());

  // “How we work” numbered steps
  const steps = ['Assess', 'Design', 'Build', 'Enable'];
  steps.forEach((step) => {
    const el = screen.getByText(new RegExp(`\\b${step}\\b`, 'i'));
    expect(el).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  // “Why The Bayes Group” bullet points (keywords)
  const whyKeywords = [
    'credentialed data scientists',
    'hands-on builders',
    'vendor-neutral advice',
    'knowledge transfer',
  ];
  whyKeywords.forEach((kw) => {
    expect(screen.getByText(new RegExp(kw, 'i'))).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  // CTA band
  expect(screen.getByText(/ready to put ai to work\?/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
  // The CTA “Book a consultation” link is the second link we captured above (ctaBookBtn)
  expect(ctaBookBtn).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(ctaBookBtn).toHaveAttribute('href', '/contact');
});
```

